<div class="ncard"><a id="node-quantum-fundamentals-qubits" name="node-quantum-fundamentals-qubits"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#157/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">quantum-fundamentals-qubits</td><td class="vd"></td><td class="vd">Fundamental</td><td class="cmp vd">C:41</td><td class="yld vd">Y:52</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:12</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Quantum Mechanics Fundamentals &amp; Qubit Superposition</div><div class="ndesc">Foundational quantum physical principles: two-level quantum states (qubits), state vectors on the Bloch sphere, unitary single- and multi-qubit transformations (Pauli X/Y/Z, Hadamard, Phase, CNOT), and Einstein-Podolsky-Rosen (EPR) quantum entanglement.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">|\psi\rangle = \cos\left(\frac{\theta}{2}\right)|0\rangle + e^{i\phi}\sin\left(\frac{\theta}{2}\right)|1\rangle</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Qubit &bull; Bloch Sphere</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-quantum-algorithms-shor-grover" name="node-quantum-algorithms-shor-grover"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#158/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">quantum-algorithms-shor-grover</td><td class="vd"></td><td class="vd">Frontier</td><td class="cmp vd">C:100</td><td class="yld vd">Y:76</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:12</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Quantum Algorithms: QFT, Shor&#39;s &amp; Grover&#39;s Acceleration</div><div class="ndesc">Foundational quantum speedup algorithms utilizing quantum phase estimation and interference: Quantum Fourier Transform (QFT) running in O((log N)^2), Shor&#39;s polynomial-time prime integer factorization breaking RSA cryptography, and Grover&#39;s unstructured database search offering quadratic speedup O(sqrt(N)).</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">|j\rangle \mapsto \frac{1}{\sqrt{N}} \sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \omega^{j \cdot k} |k\rangle \quad \text{where} \quad \omega = e^{2\pi i / N}</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Quantum Fourier Transform (QFT) &bull; Shor’s Algorithm</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-quantum-hardware-qec" name="node-quantum-hardware-qec"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#159/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">quantum-hardware-qec</td><td class="vd"></td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:84</td><td class="yld vd">Y:70</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:12</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Quantum Processors, Memory &amp; Error Correction</div><div class="ndesc">Physical hardware platforms for quantum processing: Superconducting Transmon qubits (Josephson junctions), Trapped-Ion RF Paul traps, Topological Majorana zero modes, cryogenic dilution refrigerators, and fault-tolerant Quantum Error Correction (Shor&#39;s 9-qubit code and 2D Surface Codes).</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\frac{1}{T_2} = \frac{1}{2T_1} + \frac{1}{T_\phi}, \quad \rho_{01}(t) = \rho_{01}(0) e^{-t / T_2}</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Transmon Qubit &bull; Trapped Ions</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-quantum-crypto-teleportation" name="node-quantum-crypto-teleportation"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#160/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">quantum-crypto-teleportation</td><td class="vd"></td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:84</td><td class="yld vd">Y:70</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:12</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Quantum Key Distribution &amp; Cryptographic Teleportation</div><div class="ndesc">Unconditionally secure communication protocols rooted in the laws of quantum mechanics: Quantum Key Distribution (BB84 !!protocol!! with polarized photons, E91 entanglement !!protocol!!), quantum state teleportation via classical channels and EPR pairs, and privacy amplification against eavesdropping.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">|\psi\rangle_C \otimes |\Phi^+\rangle_{AB} = \frac{1}{2} \sum_{i=0}^3 |\beta_i\rangle_{CA} \otimes (\sigma_i |\psi\rangle)_B</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Quantum Key Distribution (QKD) &bull; BB84 Protocol</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-quantum-machine-learning-vqe" name="node-quantum-machine-learning-vqe"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#161/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">quantum-machine-learning-vqe</td><td class="vd"></td><td class="vd">Frontier</td><td class="cmp vd">C:100</td><td class="yld vd">Y:76</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:12</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Variational Quantum Eigensolver &amp; Quantum Machine Learning</div><div class="ndesc">Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum (NISQ) algorithms: Parameterized Quantum Circuits (PQC), Variational Quantum Eigensolver (VQE) for molecular electronic ground-state energy, Quantum Approximate Optimization @@Algorithm@@ (QAOA), Quantum Support Vector Machines (QSVM), and Quantum Neural Networks (QNN).</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\langle H \rangle(\boldsymbol{\theta}) = \langle 0 | U^\dagger(\boldsymbol{\theta}) \hat{H} U(\boldsymbol{\theta}) | 0 \rangle \ge E_0</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Variational Quantum Eigensolver (VQE) &bull; Parameterized Quantum Circuit (PQC)</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-quantum-approximate-optimization-qaoa" name="node-quantum-approximate-optimization-qaoa"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#162/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">quantum-approximate-optimization-qaoa</td><td class="vd"></td><td class="vd">Frontier</td><td class="cmp vd">C:100</td><td class="yld vd">Y:76</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:12</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA) for Arbitrage</div><div class="ndesc">Hybrid quantum-classical variational @@algorithm@@ executing alternating problem and mixer Hamiltonians on noisy intermediate-scale quantum (NISQ) processors to approximate solutions for NP-hard combinatorial logistics and arbitrage optimization.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">|\boldsymbol{\gamma}, \boldsymbol{\beta}\rangle = \prod_{k=1}^p \exp(-i \beta_k H_M) \exp(-i \gamma_k H_C) |+\rangle^{\otimes n}</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> QAOA &bull; Cost Hamiltonian (Hc)</div></div></div>
