<div class="ncard"><a id="node-cap-pacelc-theorems" name="node-cap-pacelc-theorems"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#181/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">cap-pacelc-theorems</td><td class="vd"></td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:84</td><td class="yld vd">Y:70</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:12</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">CAP &amp; PACELC Distributed Consistency Theorems</div><div class="ndesc">Foundational theoretical trade-offs in distributed systems: Brewer&#39;s CAP Theorem (under network partitions, a distributed system must choose Consistency or @@Availability@@) and Abadi&#39;s PACELC Theorem (if Partition, choose @@Availability@@ or Consistency; Else, choose @@Latency@@ or Consistency).</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">R + W &gt; N \quad \text{and} \quad W &gt; \frac{N}{2}</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> CAP Theorem &bull; PACELC Theorem</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-consistent-hashing-sharding" name="node-consistent-hashing-sharding"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#182/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">consistent-hashing-sharding</td><td class="vd"></td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:84</td><td class="yld vd">Y:70</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:12</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Consistent Hashing &amp; Database Sharding Strategies</div><div class="ndesc">Horizontal database @@scalability@@ patterns: Range-based vs Hash-based database sharding, shard key selection to avoid hot-spots, and Consistent Hashing rings with virtual nodes to minimize key migration when adding or removing database cluster nodes.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\mathbb{E}[\Delta K] = \frac{K}{N + 1}</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Consistent Hashing &bull; Database Sharding</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-database-caching-event-driven" name="node-database-caching-event-driven"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#183/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">database-caching-event-driven</td><td class="vd"></td><td class="vd">Intermediate</td><td class="cmp vd">C:61</td><td class="yld vd">Y:60</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:12</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Distributed Caching Strategies &amp; Asynchronous Processing</div><div class="ndesc">High-performance data path engineering: Cache-Aside (Look-Aside), Write-Through, Write-Behind (Write-Back) patterns, cache invalidation, cache stampede mitigation (probabilistic early expiration XFetch), and asynchronous event-driven decoupling via message brokers and dead-letter queues.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\Delta - \beta \cdot \ln(\text{rand}()) &gt; \text{expiry} - \text{now}</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Cache-Aside Pattern &bull; Cache Stampede</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-cloud-infrastructure-orchestration" name="node-cloud-infrastructure-orchestration"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#184/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">cloud-infrastructure-orchestration</td><td class="vd"></td><td class="vd">Intermediate</td><td class="cmp vd">C:61</td><td class="yld vd">Y:60</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:12</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Enterprise Cloud Automation &amp; Infrastructure Blueprints</div><div class="ndesc">Enterprise @@Cloud@@ Management Platform (CMP) architectures (modeled on VMware vCAC/vRealize Automation): Multi-tenant resource governance, Infrastructure as Code (IaC) blueprints, property dictionaries, dynamic resource reclamation, fabric groups, and automated approval lifecycle policies.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\eta_{\text{rec}} = \frac{\sum_{i=1}^M (1 - u_i) \cdot C_i \cdot \Delta t_i}{C_{\text{total}}}</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Service Blueprint &bull; Tenant Machine Reclamation</div></div></div>
