<div class="ncard"><a id="node-humtech-powered-exoskeleton-torque-assist-orthoses" name="node-humtech-powered-exoskeleton-torque-assist-orthoses"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#920/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">humtech-powered-exoskeleton-torque-assist-orthoses</td><td class="vd"></td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:84</td><td class="yld vd">Y:70</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:12</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Carbon-Fiber Powered Robotic Exoskeleton Torque-Assist Orthoses</div><div class="ndesc">Wearable lower-limb active biomechatronic suits coupling carbon-fiber cuffs with brushless harmonic drive motors at hip and knee joints, delivering synchronized torque assist to paraplegic and mobility-impaired users.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\tau_{total} = \tau_{bio} + \tau_{exo}, \quad \tau_{exo}(t) = G_{assist} \cdot f_{phase}(\phi_{gait}) \cdot \hat{\tau}_{biological}(t)</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Harmonic Drive Gearbox &bull; Metabolic Cost of Transport (COT)</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-humtech-cochlear-implant-electrode-arrays" name="node-humtech-cochlear-implant-electrode-arrays"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#921/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">humtech-cochlear-implant-electrode-arrays</td><td class="vd"></td><td class="vd">Frontier</td><td class="cmp vd">C:100</td><td class="yld vd">Y:76</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:12</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Intracochlear Multi-Channel Electrode Micro-Arrays &amp; Speech Processors</div><div class="ndesc">Surgically implanted neural auditory prostheses inserting flexible silicone multi-electrode carrier arrays (16-22 platinum contacts) into the scala tympani of the inner ear, directly stimulating spiral ganglion auditory nerves.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">f_{nerve}(x) = A \left( 10^{a (1 - x/L)} - k \right), \quad x \in [0, L]</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Continuous Interleaved Sampling (CIS) &bull; Spiral Ganglion Cells</div></div></div>
