<div class="ncard"><a id="node-sapm-penfield-homunculus-density-01" name="node-sapm-penfield-homunculus-density-01"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1495/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">sapm-penfield-homunculus-density-01</td><td class="vd">Neuro-Somatic Topographical Cartography</td><td class="vd">Frontier</td><td class="cmp vd">C:81</td><td class="yld vd">Y:88</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Penfield Somatosensory Cortical Homunculus Magnification &amp; Mechanoreceptor Density Mapping</div><div class="ndesc">Quantifies cortical magnification factor M(x) across primary somatosensory cortex (S1 Brodmann areas 3b/1/2) as a function of peripheral Meissner and Pacinian corpuscle innervation density and two-point discrimination thresholds.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">M(\mathbf{r}) = \frac{dA_{cortex}}{dA_{skin}(\mathbf{r})} \propto \frac{\rho_{receptor}(\mathbf{r})}{\sigma_{2pt}(\mathbf{r})^2}, \quad I_{a</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Cortical Magnification Tensor &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-sapm-hebbian-stdp-preference-02" name="node-sapm-hebbian-stdp-preference-02"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1496/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">sapm-hebbian-stdp-preference-02</td><td class="vd">Synaptic Associative Conditioning</td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:85</td><td class="yld vd">Y:91</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Hebbian Spike-Timing-Dependent Plasticity (STDP) &amp; Conditioned Preference Imprinting</div><div class="ndesc">Models how pairing novel sensory motifs or conceptual cues with peak phasic dopamine and endogenous opioid release within a 20-millisecond causal window induces long-term potentiation (LTP) in nucleus accumbens and amygdala circuits.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\frac{dw_{ij}}{dt} = \eta \cdot \delta_{DA}(t) \cdot \left[ A_+ \exp\left(-\frac{\Delta t}{\tau_+}\right) \mathbb{I}(\Delta t &gt; 0) - A_- \ex</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Three-Factor Eligibility Trace &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-sapm-dopamine-prolactin-homeostasis-03" name="node-sapm-dopamine-prolactin-homeostasis-03"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1497/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">sapm-dopamine-prolactin-homeostasis-03</td><td class="vd">Neuroendocrine Feedback Control</td><td class="vd">Expert</td><td class="cmp vd">C:89</td><td class="yld vd">Y:94</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Mesolimbic Dopamine-to-Prolactin Refractory Homeostasis &amp; Opponent-Process Dynamics</div><div class="ndesc">Formulates the Solomon-Corbit opponent-process neuroendocrine cycle where acute mesolimbic dopamine surge triggers tuberoinfundibular dopamine inhibition and pituitary prolactin elevation, enforcing homeostatic satiety and refractory recovery.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\frac{dD}{dt} = I_{stim}(t) - \alpha P(t) D(t) - \gamma_D (D - D_0), \quad \frac{dP}{dt} = \beta \mathbb{I}(D &gt; D_{peak}) - \gamma_P (P - P_</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Opponent-Process Homeostatic Clamp &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-sapm-mechanoreceptor-frequency-tuning-04" name="node-sapm-mechanoreceptor-frequency-tuning-04"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1498/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">sapm-mechanoreceptor-frequency-tuning-04</td><td class="vd">Biophysical Sensory Transduction</td><td class="vd">Frontier</td><td class="cmp vd">C:93</td><td class="yld vd">Y:97</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Pacinian &amp; Meissner Mechanoreceptor Bandpass Transfer Function (40 Hz – 250 Hz)</div><div class="ndesc">Characterizes the biomechanical impedance and bandpass filtering of rapidly adapting cutaneous corpuscles: Meissner corpuscles peak at 30–50 Hz flutter while deep Pacinian lamellae resonate at 200–250 Hz sinusoidal vibration.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">H_{Pacinian}(j\omega) = \frac{G_0 (j\omega \tau_1)^n}{\prod_{k=1}^n (1 + j\omega \tau_k)}, \quad f_{res} = \frac{1}{2\pi \sqrt{\tau_{outer}\</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Lamellar Mechanical High-Pass &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-sapm-beta-vae-preference-manifold-05" name="node-sapm-beta-vae-preference-manifold-05"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1499/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">sapm-beta-vae-preference-manifold-05</td><td class="vd">Computational Psychometrics &amp; Latent Topolog</td><td class="vd">Expert</td><td class="cmp vd">C:89</td><td class="yld vd">Y:88</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Beta-VAE Disentangled Preference Latent-Space Manifold &amp; Orthogonal Factor Discovery</div><div class="ndesc">Maps complex individual aesthetic, sensory, and roleplay preference profiles into a low-dimensional orthogonal latent space using a beta-Variational Autoencoder, separating core psychological axes (novelty, tactile intensity, power-symmetry, narrative context).</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\mathcal{L}_{\beta\text{-VAE}}(\theta, \phi) = \mathbb{E}_{q_\phi(\mathbf{z}|\mathbf{x})}[\ln p_\theta(\mathbf{x} \mid \mathbf{z})] - \beta </span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Total Correlation Disentanglement &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-sapm-autonomic-bifurcation-cusp-06" name="node-sapm-autonomic-bifurcation-cusp-06"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1500/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">sapm-autonomic-bifurcation-cusp-06</td><td class="vd">Nonlinear Autonomic Nervous System Dynamics</td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:93</td><td class="yld vd">Y:91</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Parasympathetic-to-Sympathetic Autonomic Phase Transition &amp; Zeeman Catastrophe Cusp</div><div class="ndesc">Models the physiological transition from vasodilatory parasympathetic build-up (pelvic splanchnic nerve) to rhythmic sympathetic spinal reflex discharge as a fold/cusp bifurcation on a Thom-Zeeman potential surface.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">V(x; a, b) = \frac{1}{4} x^4 + \frac{1}{2} a x^2 + b x, \quad \Delta_{bif} = 8 a^3 + 27 b^2 = 0 \implies \text{Spinal Reflex Cascade}</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Autonomic Cusp Bifurcation &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
