<div class="ncard"><a id="node-goop-section321-deminimis-partition-02" name="node-goop-section321-deminimis-partition-02"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1538/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">goop-section321-deminimis-partition-02</td><td class="vd">Customs Threshold Optimization</td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:85</td><td class="yld vd">Y:91</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Section 321 / De Minimis Customs Threshold Partitioning &amp; Duty-Zero Knapsack</div><div class="ndesc">Solves a 0-1 Multi-Knapsack problem that partitions multi-item international orders across discrete daily shipment manifests so each parcel’s declared customs value remains strictly below statutory duty-free de minimis ceilings (e.g. $800 US Section 321).</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\min_{\{S_1,\dots,S_K\}} \sum_{k=1}^K \left[ F_{base} + c_{kg} W(S_k) + \tau_{HS} V(S_k) \mathbb{I}\left(V(S_k) &gt; V_{\text{de\_minimis}}\rig</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Section 321 Knapsack Split &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-goop-phash-clip-oem-tracing-03" name="node-goop-phash-clip-oem-tracing-03"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1539/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">goop-phash-clip-oem-tracing-03</td><td class="vd">Supply-Chain Visual OSINT</td><td class="vd">Expert</td><td class="cmp vd">C:89</td><td class="yld vd">Y:94</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Perceptual Hash (pHash) &amp; CLIP Visual Embedding OSINT for OEM/ODM Factory Tracing</div><div class="ndesc">Strips boutique D2C brand watermarks from product photography and queries 512-dim CLIP / DCT perceptual hashes against 1688, Alibaba, and Panjiva bill-of-lading registries to locate the exact original equipment manufacturer (OEM) selling the identical item at 1/5th cost.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">S_{OEM}(I_{D2C}, I_{factory}) = \lambda \frac{\mathbf{e}_{CLIP}(I_{D2C}) \cdot \mathbf{e}_{CLIP}(I_{fac})}{\|\mathbf{e}_{D2C}\| \|\mathbf{e}</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> ODM Mold Perceptual Tracing &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-goop-fx-dcc-interbank-routing-04" name="node-goop-fx-dcc-interbank-routing-04"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1540/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">goop-fx-dcc-interbank-routing-04</td><td class="vd">Foreign Exchange Microstructure</td><td class="vd">Frontier</td><td class="cmp vd">C:93</td><td class="yld vd">Y:97</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Dynamic Currency Conversion (DCC) Avoidance &amp; Interbank Mid-Market FX Routing</div><div class="ndesc">Eliminates the 3.5%–7.0% predatory Dynamic Currency Conversion (DCC) markup embedded in global checkout gateways by forcing settlement in the merchant’s native local currency (JPY, EUR, CNY, GBP) routed through zero-markup Visa/Mastercard interbank or Wise multi-currency rails.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\Delta C_{FX} = P_{local} \cdot \left( e_{DCC}^{\text{checkout}} - e_{spot}^{\text{interbank}}(1 + s_{rail}) \right), \quad s_{rail} \le 0.0</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Native-Currency Settlement Rule &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
