<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-thaler-sunstein-choice-architecture-01" name="node-beff-thaler-sunstein-choice-architecture-01"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1551/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-thaler-sunstein-choice-architecture-01</td><td class="vd">Environmental Nudge Engineering</td><td class="vd">Frontier</td><td class="cmp vd">C:81</td><td class="yld vd">Y:88</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Thaler-Sunstein Domestic Choice Architecture &amp; Caloric Friction-Asymmetry Design</div><div class="ndesc">Re-architects home kitchen and living defaults so nutrient-dense, high-protein whole foods have zero preparation friction (eye-level clear glass, pre-prepped) while hyper-palatable processed foods require high activation energy (absent from home inventory), shifting daily energy balance by -400 kcal with zero willpower depletion.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">P(\text{Choice}_i) = \frac{\exp\left( \beta (U_i - \kappa E_{\text{friction}, i}) \right)}{\sum_{j} \exp\left( \beta (U_j - \kappa E_{\text{</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Activation-Energy Friction Asymmetry &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-dyadic-exercise-markov-contagion-02" name="node-beff-dyadic-exercise-markov-contagion-02"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1552/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-dyadic-exercise-markov-contagion-02</td><td class="vd">Shared Physical Training Dynamics</td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:85</td><td class="yld vd">Y:91</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Coupled Dyadic Resistance-Training Markov Chain &amp; Leader-Initiated Adherence Contagion</div><div class="ndesc">Models how one partner’s consistent, joyful, zero-pressure invitation into strength and mobility training shifts the partner’s adherence transition matrix: empirical Christakis-Fowler dyadic health studies prove partner exercise adoption rises by 340% when the initiator models consistency first.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">P(A_{F, t+1}=1 \mid A_{M, t}=1) = p_0 + \gamma_{couple} \cdot \mathbb{I}(\text{ZeroCriticism}) \cdot \mathbb{I}(\text{SharedRitual}) \gg P(A</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Reactance-Free Behavioral Modeling &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-rusbult-investment-fidelity-03" name="node-beff-rusbult-investment-fidelity-03"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1553/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-rusbult-investment-fidelity-03</td><td class="vd">Game-Theoretic Relational Fidelity</td><td class="vd">Expert</td><td class="cmp vd">C:89</td><td class="yld vd">Y:94</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Rusbult Investment Model of Commitment ($C = S - A + I$) &amp; Structural Fidelity Lock</div><div class="ndesc">Formalizes Caryl Rusbult’s empirical Investment Model: long-term relational fidelity is maximized by simultaneously elevating relational Satisfaction (S), increasing shared non-transferable Investments (I), and naturally eclipsing perceived quality of Alternatives (A).</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">C(t) = w_S S(t) - w_A A(t) + w_I I(t), \quad \mathbb{P}(\text{Fidelity} \mid C) = \frac{1}{1 + \exp(-\lambda (C(t) - C_{crit}))} \to 1</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Rusbult Commitment Inequality &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-circadian-zeitgeber-alignment-04" name="node-beff-circadian-zeitgeber-alignment-04"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1554/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-circadian-zeitgeber-alignment-04</td><td class="vd">Chronobiological Metabolic Coupling</td><td class="vd">Frontier</td><td class="cmp vd">C:93</td><td class="yld vd">Y:97</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Shared Circadian Zeitgeber Entrainment: Morning Lux, Sleep Synchrony &amp; Leptin-Ghrelin Balance</div><div class="ndesc">Synchronizes the couple’s suprachiasmatic nucleus (SCN) master clock via morning 10,000-lux outdoor walks and aligned 10:30 PM sleep onset: simultaneous bedtime boosts relationship satisfaction AND normalizes leptin/ghrelin ratio to prevent late-night cortisol snacking.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\Delta \phi_{sleep} = |\phi_M - \phi_F| \to 0 \implies \frac{[\text{Ghrelin}]}{[\text{Leptin}]} = R_0 \exp\left( \alpha \max(0, 7.5\text{h} </span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Dyadic Zeitgeber Synchrony &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-praise-dopamine-vs-cortisol-05" name="node-beff-praise-dopamine-vs-cortisol-05"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1555/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-praise-dopamine-vs-cortisol-05</td><td class="vd">Neuroendocrine Behavioral Shaping</td><td class="vd">Expert</td><td class="cmp vd">C:89</td><td class="yld vd">Y:88</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Operant Positive-Reinforcement Shaping vs. Cortisol-Driven Stress Eating Avoidance</div><div class="ndesc">Proves why criticizing a partner’s body or habits backfires biochemically: interpersonal criticism spikes HPA-axis cortisol and neuropeptide Y (NPY), which directly stimulates visceral adipogenesis and comfort-food cravings, whereas sincere praise of micro-wins fuels dopaminergic adherence.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\frac{dM_{visc}}{dt} \propto [\text{Cortisol}] \cdot [\text{NPY}] \cdot \mathbb{I}(\text{Criticism}), \quad \frac{dH_{fit}}{dt} = \eta_{DA} </span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Cortisol-NPY Lipogenic Loop &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-protein-leverage-neat-habitat-06" name="node-beff-protein-leverage-neat-habitat-06"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1556/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-protein-leverage-neat-habitat-06</td><td class="vd">Nutritional &amp; Metabolic Biophysics</td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:93</td><td class="yld vd">Y:91</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Simpson-Raubenheimer Protein-Leverage Hypothesis &amp; High-NEAT Lifestyle Topology</div><div class="ndesc">Applies the Simpson-Raubenheimer Protein-Leverage equation: organisms continue eating until reaching their absolute daily protein target P*; structuring shared gourmet meals around 35%+ protein calorie density plus walkable dates naturally caps total caloric intake without hunger.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">E_{total} = \frac{P_{target}^*}{p_{\%}} - \text{NEAT}_{walk}, \quad \frac{\partial E_{total}}{\partial p_{\%}} = -\frac{P_{target}^*}{p_{\%}</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Protein-Leverage Satiety Floor &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-aron-self-expansion-novelty-07" name="node-beff-aron-self-expansion-novelty-07"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1557/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-aron-self-expansion-novelty-07</td><td class="vd">Novelty-Driven Fidelity Reinforcement</td><td class="vd">Frontier</td><td class="cmp vd">C:97</td><td class="yld vd">Y:94</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Arthur Aron Self-Expansion Model &amp; Shared High-Arousal Adventure Bonding</div><div class="ndesc">Implements Arthur Aron’s Self-Expansion paradigm: engaging in novel, physically active adventures together (hiking, skiing, dancing, travel, martial arts) floods the pair-bond with endogenous norepinephrine and dopamine, vaccinating the relationship against boredom-driven infidelity.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">S_{boredom}(t) = S_0 \exp\left( -\int_0^t \lambda_{novelty} A_{\text{shared}}(\tau)\,d\tau \right), \quad \mathbb{P}(\text{Drift}) \propto S</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Aron Self-Expansion Vaccine &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-digital-attention-boundary-08" name="node-beff-digital-attention-boundary-08"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1558/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-digital-attention-boundary-08</td><td class="vd">Social-Media Boundary Architecture</td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:83</td><td class="yld vd">Y:97</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Digital Validation-Loop Hygiene &amp; Mutual Attention-Allocation Conservation</div><div class="ndesc">Models how external algorithmic validation engines (infinite DM/thirst-trap feedback loops) siphon finite social-dopamine bandwidth away from the primary bond, and establishes reciprocal, high-trust digital boundaries and phone-free sanctuary hours.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">B_{total} = I_{\text{dyad}}(t) + \sum_{k \in \mathcal{S}_{ext}} I_{\text{validation}, k}(t), \quad \sum_{k} I_{\text{validation}, k} \to 0 \</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Reciprocal Sanctuary Protocol &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-cooperative-milestone-gamification-09" name="node-beff-cooperative-milestone-gamification-09"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1559/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-cooperative-milestone-gamification-09</td><td class="vd">Behavioral Incentive Design</td><td class="vd">Expert</td><td class="cmp vd">C:87</td><td class="yld vd">Y:88</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Cooperative Fitness Gamification &amp; Joint Milestone Reward Escrow</div><div class="ndesc">Links shared 90-day fitness and body-composition habits (daily step counts, strength sessions, cooking streaks) to celebratory shared experiential rewards (spa retreats, wardrobe upgrades, beach travel) where both partners win together as a 2-player co-op team.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">U_{today} = -c_{workout} + \gamma_{\text{streak}} V_{\text{reward}} \cdot \mathbb{P}\left(\text{Streak}_M = N \wedge \text{Streak}_F = N\rig</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Two-Player Co-Op Streak Lock &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-oxytocin-affection-baseline-10" name="node-beff-oxytocin-affection-baseline-10"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1560/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-oxytocin-affection-baseline-10</td><td class="vd">Neurobiological Pair-Bond Maintenance</td><td class="vd">Frontier</td><td class="cmp vd">C:91</td><td class="yld vd">Y:91</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Non-Transactional Affection Baseline &amp; C-Tactile Afferent Oxytocin Saturation</div><div class="ndesc">Maintains continuous C-tactile unmyelinated fiber stimulation (6-second embraces, 20-second kisses, spontaneous non-demanding touch at 3 cm/s velocity) to keep central oxytocin concentration above the pair-bond fidelity threshold 24/7.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">f_{CT}(v) = f_{max} \exp\left(-\frac{(\ln v - \ln v_{opt})^2}{2\sigma_v^2}\right), \quad [\text{OXT}]_{ss} = \frac{k_{CT} N_{touch} f_{CT}(v</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> C-Tactile Affective Bandwidth &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-christakis-fowler-social-norm-11" name="node-beff-christakis-fowler-social-norm-11"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1561/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-christakis-fowler-social-norm-11</td><td class="vd">Sociometric Network Selection</td><td class="vd">Expert</td><td class="cmp vd">C:87</td><td class="yld vd">Y:94</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Christakis-Fowler 3-Degree Social Network Contagion &amp; High-Fidelity Peer Clustering</div><div class="ndesc">Applies Christakis and Fowler’s Framingham Heart Study network math: both obesity (+57% risk per friend) and divorce (+75% risk per divorced close friend) propagate across 3 degrees of social separation; curating a social circle of fit, happily committed couples stabilizes both metrics.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\mathbf{y}_{t+1} = \rho_{net} \mathbf{W}_{friends} \mathbf{y}_t + \mathbf{X}\boldsymbol{\beta} + \boldsymbol{\varepsilon}, \quad \bar{y}_{\m</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Three-Degree Norm Gravity &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-endocrine-mitochondrial-habitat-12" name="node-beff-endocrine-mitochondrial-habitat-12"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1562/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-endocrine-mitochondrial-habitat-12</td><td class="vd">Environmental Biochemistry</td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:91</td><td class="yld vd">Y:97</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Domestic Xenoestrogen/Endocrine-Disruptor Purge &amp; Mitochondrial Vitality Optimization</div><div class="ndesc">Eliminates household endocrine-disrupting chemicals (phthalates, BPA/BPS plastics, synthetic fragrance xenoestrogens, seed-oil lipid peroxides) while optimizing magnesium, D3/K2, omega-3, and iron status to support healthy endogenous hormone balance, energy, and libido.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\theta_{endo} = \frac{[H] / K_H}{1 + [H]/K_H + \sum_j [X_{EDC, j}] / K_{EDC, j}}, \quad [X_{EDC, j}] \to 0 \implies \theta_{endo} \to \theta</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Xenoestrogen Receptor Unblocking &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-reciprocal-mate-value-lock-13" name="node-beff-reciprocal-mate-value-lock-13"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1563/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-reciprocal-mate-value-lock-13</td><td class="vd">Evolutionary Game Stability</td><td class="vd">Frontier</td><td class="cmp vd">C:95</td><td class="yld vd">Y:88</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Assortative Mate-Value Trajectory Lock &amp; Leader-First Self-Improvement</div><div class="ndesc">Proves that in any dyadic game, the single highest-leverage control variable for inspiring a partner’s peak fitness and devotion is continuously elevating one’s own physical fitness, emotional mastery, and mission competence first.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">\frac{dV_F}{dt} = \kappa_{track} \max(0,\, V_M(t) - V_F(t)) + g_0, \quad \frac{dV_M}{dt} = u_{\text{self\_mastery}}(t) &gt; 0</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> Assortative Trajectory Pull &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
<div class="ncard"><a id="node-beff-sdt-autonomous-motivation-14" name="node-beff-sdt-autonomous-motivation-14"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1564/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">beff-sdt-autonomous-motivation-14</td><td class="vd">Intrinsic Psychological Sustainability</td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:91</td><td class="yld vd">Y:91</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Deci-Ryan Self-Determination Theory (Autonomy, Competence, Relatedness) Internalization</div><div class="ndesc">Guarantees that fitness and fidelity behaviors become 100% self-sustaining by satisfying Deci and Ryan’s three innate psychological nutrients—Autonomy (free choice, zero coercion), Competence (progressive mastery), and Relatedness (warm partnership).</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">M_{\text{intrinsic}} = A_{\text{autonomy}}^{\alpha} \cdot C_{\text{competence}}^{\beta} \cdot R_{\text{relatedness}}^{\gamma}, \quad A_{\tex</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> SDT Multiplicative Autonomy Gate &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
