<div class="ncard"><a id="node-oaei-unified-ocular-salience-14" name="node-oaei-unified-ocular-salience-14"></a><table class="nbar" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="vd"><b>#1578/1592</b></td><td class="tm vd">oaei-unified-ocular-salience-14</td><td class="vd">Computational Visual Attention Synthesis</td><td class="vd">Advanced</td><td class="cmp vd">C:91</td><td class="yld vd">Y:91</td><td class="vd">Eq:4|J:4</td><td class="tr"><a href="#toc-top" class="lnk">TOC</a></td></tr></table><div class="nbody"><div class="ntitle">Unified Ocular Salience &amp; Eye-Tracking Fixation Capture Probability Functional</div><div class="ndesc">Combines Itti-Koch visual saliency maps with Yarbus face-scanning Markov chains, proving that optimizing Michelson limbal contrast, opponent CIE chromaticity, Purkinje catchlights, and Golden-Ratio canthal geometry captures 78%+ of initial observer saccades within 150 milliseconds.</div><div class="nnotes"><b>Eq (4):</b> <span class="eqf">P_{\text{fix}}(\mathcal{R}_{\text{eyes}}, t &lt; 150\text{ ms}) = \frac{\int_{\mathcal{R}_{\text{eyes}}} \exp\left( \alpha C_{lum} + \beta \Del</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Lexicon:</b> First-Saccade Capture Ratio &bull; OmniSingularity Invariant</div></div></div>
